# Concrete HS normalizer geometry for I.2.2(5)

The actual normalizer core has C₄³ coordinates; its involutions and binary
square quotient are identified with the marked elementary eight and its
existing normalizer action. Its order-two elements are two-central in HS.
The normalizer is perfect, has odd index, and admits the required fixed-free
order-seven action; all quotient involutions are conjugate by the normalizer.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith I.2.2(5), final HS paragraph, printed p.412 / PDF p.423.
The concrete alternating preimage, pair kernel and cyclic factor are identified
with the actual residual X₀, core R₀ and center V₀. Thus A ≤ X₀, V₀ normally
generates the normalizer core, and the elementary eight lies in R₀. The marked
two-central involution j₀ lies in the normalizer and R₀ but outside A, and its
quotient image represents every quotient involution class. The exact omega
image and Sylow-seven action discharge the complete abelian-section model input.
No covering-group conclusion is assumed.
-/
